    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $s=\\sin15^\\circ$. Show that $s=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}2$.\n\nUse $\\cos30^\\circ=1-2s^2$ and take the positive square root.",
          "worked": "Substitute $\\theta=15^\\circ$ into the supplied identity:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos30^\\circ&=1-2s^2\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}2&=1-2s^2\\\\2s^2&=1-\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\\\s^2&=\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}4.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $15^\\circ$ is acute, $s>0$. Therefore $s=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Expand and simplify $\\dfrac{(\\sqrt3-1)^2}2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2-\\sqrt3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^2}2&=\\frac{3-2\\sqrt3+1}2\\\\\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^2}2&=\\frac{4-2\\sqrt3}2\\\\\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^2}2&=2-\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-p2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $\\sin15^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sin15^\\circ=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}$.\n\nUse part (b) to simplify the square root in part (a).",
          "worked": "Using parts (a) and (b),\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin15^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}2\\\\\\sin15^\\circ&=\\frac12\\sqrt{\\frac{(\\sqrt3-1)^2}2}\\\\\\sin15^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt3-1}{2\\sqrt2}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe final square root uses $\\sqrt3-1>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
